167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1-Image Filtering: Utilize filtering techniques, such as Median filtering, to reduce or remove noise and enhance the overall quality of the images. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2- Assessment of Image Quality: This involves evaluating the overall quality of the old image, including factors such as fading, loss of detail, discoloration, and blurriness.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3-Selection of Restoration Techniques: Based on the identified imperfections and restoration goals, appropriate techniques are chosen. These may include sharpening, noise reduction, contrast enhancement, scratch removal, color correction, and unsharp image restoration.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
